Adapt RDO's rpm-master python-oslo-utils.spec to the released 2026.1 tarball
(oslo.utils 10.0.1).

    error: Failed build dependencies:
        python3dist(tzdata) >= 2022.4 is needed by python-oslo-utils-10.0.1

tzdata appears only in oslo.utils's test-requirements.txt, not in
requirements.txt, so it is a test dependency and not a runtime one. Nothing on
EL10 provides python3dist(tzdata): Rocky ships the system tzdata package, which
is what zoneinfo actually reads, and does not package the PyPI fallback. Added
to the spec's own excluded_brs list, which is the mechanism it already uses for
exactly this - the list is applied to test-requirements.txt in %prep.

diff -ur a/oslo-utils/python-oslo-utils.spec b/oslo-utils/python-oslo-utils.spec
--- a/python-oslo-utils.spec	2026-09-28 17:10:58.093140565 +0000
+++ b/python-oslo-utils.spec	2026-09-28 17:20:03.724438915 +0000
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@
 %{?dlrn: %global tarsources oslo.utils}
 %{!?dlrn: %global tarsources oslo_utils}
 # we are excluding some BRs from automatic generator
-%global excluded_brs doc8 bandit pre-commit hacking flake8-import-order
+%global excluded_brs tzdata doc8 bandit pre-commit hacking flake8-import-order
 # Exclude sphinx from BRs if docs are disabled
 %if ! 0%{?with_doc}
 %global excluded_brs %{excluded_brs} sphinx openstackdocstheme
